LANE-ASK wiring patch: route the seven canonical Ask FYD questions through
the evidence-graded concierge (src/fyd/ask/concierge.ts, new file, already in
the tree and tested).

WHAT IT DOES
------------
In composeAskFyd (src/fyd/ask/answer.ts), after site-patch intent detection
and before the generic composer, questions matching one of the seven
canonical concierge questions are answered by answerConciergeQuestion and
converted with toAskFydAnswer onto the existing AskAnswer-shaped pieces
(answer text with [n] markers, evidenceRefs, claimClassifications, unknowns).
Everything else keeps the existing composer. The route
(src/app/api/fyd/ask/ask-pipeline.ts) and the widget
(src/fyd/components/ask-fyd-widget.tsx) need no changes: they already render
answer/evidenceRefs/claimClassifications/unknowns, and the 3-class reducer
(answerClassFor) maps the concierge grades onto supported/derived/unknown
(SUPPORTED -> supported, DERIVED/INFERRED -> derived, all-UNKNOWN -> unknown
refusal).

EFFECT ON THE 7 QUESTIONS x 2 SITES
------------------------------------
- "What does this business do?" -> profile answer quoting the description.
- "What services do they offer?" -> one SUPPORTED claim per service object
  plus a DERIVED count claim, all cited.
- "Where do they operate?" -> SUPPORTED location / service-area claims.
- "Who works here?" -> SUPPORTED person record + INFERRED username reading
  + UNKNOWN real name (coppersmith); UNKNOWN refusal (happy-place).
- "How do you know?" -> the evidence chain (record, source, date, basis).
- "What information conflicts?" -> DERIVED "no conflicts found" on both
  sites today; contradictions surface with both values cited when present.
- "What don't you know?" -> the probed facts with no evidence, as UNKNOWN.

SAFETY
------
- matchConciergeQuestion returns null for everything else, so non-canonical
  questions (proposals, replies, open-ended) keep the exact current behavior.
- The concierge reads only ctx.base (the already-visibility-projected public
  graph); no new data access, no grants, no proposals (proposal: null).
- The module throws on a SUPPORTED/DERIVED/INFERRED claim without evidence
  instead of rendering it; the pipeline's catch-all maps that to an honest
  500 unknown, never a half-graded answer.

